    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To expand the product \\((2x+3)(x+5)\\), we will use the distributive property, also known as the FOIL method for binomials. The distributive property states that \\((a+b)(c+d) = ac + ad + bc + bd\\).\n\nHere, \\(a = 2x\\), \\(b = 3\\), \\(c = x\\), and \\(d = 5\\). Applying the distributive property, we get:\n\n\\[\n(2x+3)(x+5) = (2x)(x) + (2x)(5) + (3)(x) + (3)(5)\n\\]\n\nNow, we will perform each of the multiplications:\n\n\\[\n(2x)(x) = 2x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n(2x)(5) = 10x\n\\]\n\\[\n(3)(x) = 3x\n\\]\n\\[\n(3)(5) = 15\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine all these terms together:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15\n\\]\n\nWe can combine the like terms \\(10x\\) and \\(3x\\):\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 13x + 15\n\\]\n\nThus, the expanded form of \\((2x+3)(x+5)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2x^2 + 13x + 15}\n\\]",
